  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Food Science and Technology A.S. Degree - Cal-GETC GE' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published September 22, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7794/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: Cal-GETC. Official Total Units: 75-77; this seed models the first-listed/recommended path = 16 + 16 + 6 + 17 + 15 + 6 = 76 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page; STAT C1000 at 4 units, first-listed in the ME slot). Semester sums verified against the map's 16-17 / 16 / 6 / 17 / 14-15 / 6 headers. The two Summer Terms are labeled 'Summer Term (Year 1)' and 'Summer Term (Year 2)' (the map prints 'Summer Term' for both). Choice slots: (1) ENGL C1000 / 488 / H+ ESLW 340, Area 1A — ENGL C1000 selected; (2) ME NUTRI 300 / H 480 Nutrition (3) — NUTRI 300 selected; (3) ME STAT C1000 / C1000H / PSYC 330 / ECON 310 (3-4) — STAT C1000 selected at 4 units (first-listed). In-plan prereqs: CHEM 401 requires CHEM 400; MATH 401 requires MATH 400; CHEM 423 requires CHEM 401; BIOL 402 requires CHEM 400; BIOL 440 requires CHEM 305/309/400 (CHEM 400 in-plan); PHYS 360 requires PHYS 350 — all with grades of 'C' or better. Documented (external) prereqs: CHEM 400 requires CHEM 300 with a 'C' or better within one year or ACS placement AND Intermediate Algebra; MATH 400 requires MATH 372 & 373, or 375, or 386 with 'C' or better, or placement (students not placing directly take the MATHS 60/MATH 400 combo); PHYS 350 requires high school trigonometry or equivalent or MATH 373 with 'C' or better (in-plan MATH 400 exceeds this); STAT C1000 not placed directly -> STAT 10/STAT C1000 or STAT 10/PSYC 330 combo (spring only); ECON 310 requires Intermediate Algebra; students not placing directly in ENGL C1000 take the ENGL 80/ENGL C1000 combo; ENGL 488 requires ESL 325; ESLW 340 requires ESL 325 or Los Rios assessment placement. Map note: many math/science courses have prerequisites and may take longer than this sequence. Area 4 rule: the Summer Term (Year 2) Area 4 course must be from a different discipline than the Summer Term (Year 1) Area 4 course. AA requirements: 60 degree-applicable units with 2.0 GPA, 12 units within Los Rios, each required course 'C' or better, Cal-GETC Areas 1-6 with 'C' or better. Nutrition & Food Science Department, Health & Health Professions Meta Majors. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
